<section class="eh-shift">
  <div class="eh-shift-row">
    <div class="eh-shift-lead">
      <p class="eh-shift-lead-text">There are new events now, with higher volume, velocity, and variety.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="eh-shift-detail">
      <p class="eh-shift-detail-text">The world now produces events in higher volume, at higher velocity, and in more variety than a few years ago. Most maps &mdash; the warehouse, the reports, the dashboards &mdash; are revised once a year, at the regular planning cycle. When events move faster than that, parts of the map fall behind without anyone deciding that they should. <span class="eh-shift-accent">Is your map &mdash; data, infrastructure, analytics &mdash; updated often enough to keep up?</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="eh-shift-row">
    <div class="eh-shift-lead">
      <p class="eh-shift-lead-text">Signals now arrive before the reports that are meant to explain them.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="eh-shift-detail">
      <p class="eh-shift-detail-text">A supplier delay shows up in a chat thread, a sensor log, or a news alert days before it reaches the monthly report. By the time the official number lands, the decision it was meant to inform has often already been made. <span class="eh-shift-accent">How long is the gap between when something happens and when your reports admit it?</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="eh-shift-row">
    <div class="eh-shift-lead">
      <p class="eh-shift-lead-text">Many of the events that matter most were never part of the original design.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="eh-shift-detail">
      <p class="eh-shift-detail-text">Data models are built around the questions people knew to ask at the time. New products, new channels, and new risks generate events that fall outside those models, so they are dropped, flattened into an &ldquo;other&rdquo; bucket, or never captured at all. <span class="eh-shift-accent">Which events in your business have no place to land?</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="eh-shift-row">
    <div class="eh-shift-lead">
      <p class="eh-shift-lead-text">Faster data does not help if the questions are still from last year.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="eh-shift-detail">
      <p class="eh-shift-detail-text">Streaming pipelines and real-time dashboards can shrink latency to seconds, but they still answer the questions that were written into them. When the environment shifts, the speed is applied to the wrong measures. <span class="eh-shift-accent">When did you last change what you measure, not just how quickly you measure it?</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
```

